Rama reaches lotus-filled Pampa with Lakshmana --- Rama praises flowering Pampa woods to Lakshmana --- Spring breeze birds and blossoms inflame grieving Rama --- Rama envies mating peacocks and calls spring unbearable without Sita --- Rama reads crow cry as Sita messenger --- Lotus buds recall Sita eyes and breeze recalls her sigh --- Rama mourns deer with does while parted from doe-eyed Sita --- Rama eyes fair Pampa and marches toward Rishyamuka
